        <body>
            <div xml:id="d116">

                <pb facs="0230" n="168" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg168"/>

                <head>No. 111.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Noyes to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-12-21"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 21, 1877</date>.
                        (Received January 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 44.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    translation of the message of President McMahon, delivered to the Senate and
                    Chamber of Deputies on Friday last, but received at too late an hour to be sent
                    in the last dispatch-bag. It is a document which has been received with general
                    satisfaction as marking by a solemn declaration the sincere acceptance by the
                    Chief of State of real parliamentary government in France, and as a permanent
                    solution of the long and harassing series of ministerial crises which have
                    marked the struggles of parties during the past seven months.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDWARD F. NOYES.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d116-a1.xml" xpointer="d116-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
